{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "trace_id": "reduced_to_full_revert",
  "description": "Reversion from reduced salience back to full, and the hysteresis dead band on the way. The learner reaches quorum at full salience and advances; under the reduced cue only half the corners rebuild, so the qualified share settles at exactly 0.5 - neither at the 0.75 advance threshold nor below the 0.5 revert threshold - and the element holds there for several laps, which is what the asymmetric thresholds are for. When the two remaining corners regress and de-qualify on their second consecutive failure, the share falls to 0 and the element reverts. The reversion does NOT reset the evidence windows (framing v6): the depleted evidence that fell below quorum is exactly what the learner has to rebuild to advance again.",
